   TThhee nnaammeessppaacceess AAPPII
       As well as various _/_p_r_o_c files described below, the namespaces API
       includes the following system calls:

       cclloonnee(2)
              The  cclloonnee(2)  system  call creates a new process.  If the _f_l_a_g_s
              argument of the call specifies one or  more  of  the  CCLLOONNEE__NNEEWW**
              flags  listed  above,  then  new namespaces are created for each
              flag,  and  the  child  process  is  made  a  member  of   those
              namespaces.   (This  system  call  also  implements  a number of
              features unrelated to namespaces.)

       sseettnnss(2)
              The sseettnnss(2) system call allows the calling process to  join  an
              existing  namespace.   The  namespace to join is specified via a
              file descriptor that refers to one  of  the  _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_n_s  files
              described below.

       uunnsshhaarree(2)
              The  uunnsshhaarree(2)  system  call moves the calling process to a new
              namespace.  If the _f_l_a_g_s argument of the call specifies  one  or
              more  of  the CCLLOONNEE__NNEEWW** flags listed above, then new namespaces
              are created for each flag, and the calling  process  is  made  a
              member of those namespaces.  (This system call also implements a
              number of features unrelated to namespaces.)

       iiooccttll(2)
              Various  iiooccttll(2) operations can be used to discover information
              about   namespaces.    These   operations   are   described   in
              iiooccttll__nnssffss(2).

       Creation  of new namespaces using cclloonnee(2) and uunnsshhaarree(2) in most cases
       requires the CCAAPP__SSYYSS__AADDMMIINN capability, since, in the new namespace, the
       creator will have the power to change global resources that are visible
       to other processes that  are  subsequently  created  in,  or  join  the
       namespace.   User  namespaces  are  the  exception: since Linux 3.8, no
       privilege is required to create a user namespace.

